  "comments": "<p><i>Obverse</i><br>Die <strong>1</strong> - squat letters in legend, '1' without nose, '9' in date with widely open tail.<br>Die <strong>2</strong> - tall letters in legend, '1' with nose, '9' in date with less open tail.<br>Picture: © Images courtesy of Alexandr Prokofyev.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/61c8ee2f4e83c.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/61c8ee2f4e83c.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br><i>Combinations</i><br><strong>1</strong>: 1984, 1985, 1986, 1986 PS, 1987, 1988, 1988 PS.<br><strong>2</strong>: 1986.<br><br><i>Abbreviation</i><br>PS - Proof set.<br><br><i>Note</i>. Die <strong>2</strong> became a model for reduced size coinage in 1989-1990 (N# 22678).</p>",
